To multiply two integers, repeatedly add or subtact one integer from zero. Adding or subtracting as many times as the other integer
  EX: 15 x 4
      x0  x1   x2   x3   x4
      0 + 15 + 15 + 15 + 15
      15 x 4 = 60
  EX2: 12 x -4
       x0 x-1 x-2 x-3 x-4
       0 -12 -12 -12 -12
       12 x -4 = 48
